  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/... \nThe ridge is forecast to weaken Sunday into Monday with H5 \nheights dropping to 594-596dm or right around the 90th percentile\nof climatology. Despite the ridge weakening, the residual heat \ndome will take some time to cool as forecast highs Monday only \ndrop a couple degrees from Sunday's readings, keeping the HeatRisk\nat Major to Extreme for much of the area. As the ridge weakens \nand also shifts its orientation some, moisture should begin to \nincrease again across southeast Arizona on Sunday and then \neventually over all of southern and central Arizona Monday into \nTuesday. As a result, convective potential will tick upwards early\nnext week, first over the Arizona higher terrain and eventually \ninto the lower deserts during the middle part of next week. The \nexpected increase in convection is likely to help to cool things \noff Tuesday into Wednesday, dropping the HeatRisk into a high-end\nModerate to low-end Major. There is still a good amount of \nuncertainty as far as the storm chances during the first half of \nnext week, so any delay in the moisture may result in having to \nextend the Extreme Heat Warning another day or so for portions of \nthe area.",
